            <ArticleTitle>Validity of the General Health Questionnaire (GHQ) in detecting psychiatric disturbance in amputees with phantom pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>277-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The 28-item General Health Questionnaire (GHQ) was validated against the PSE-derived Index of Definition in a sample of amputees with long-standing phantom and stump pain attending a Limb Fitting Centre. This form of the GHQ is a sensitive identifier of overt psychiatric disorder in this setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
